/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# The generated perf fixture (fixtures/perf/README.md). Outside target/ on
# purpose: the Rust build cache manages that directory, and on CI it restored a
# partial copy that the generator then tried to reuse.
/.perf-fixture

# Self-measurement artefacts (scripts/self-measure.sh). Written into the working
# tree rather than under .git because CI uploads them as a build artefact and a
# reader needs a path to point at — but they are outputs, not sources, and a
# dogfood run must never show up as a dirty tree in the measurement that follows
# it.
/andon-self-measure.txt
/andon-self-measure.html
/andon-self-measure.json

# Ephemeral agent worktrees (EnterWorktree, `claude --worktree`, subagent isolation).
# Native tooling creates and sweeps these; they are checkouts of this same repo, so
# committing them would nest the tree inside itself. Durable, human-named worktrees
# live outside the repo under the project's `wt/` directory instead — see
# gowtham-workflow/docs/PROJECT-LAYOUT.md. Never symlink or junction this path.
/.claude/worktrees/
